BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:das-minsk-culinary-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260906
SUMMARY:Deadline: DAS MINSK Culinary Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:DAS MINSK opened in 1977 as a terrace restaurant and now runs a
 s a museum of modern and contemporary art\, and its Culinary Residency bui
 lds on that history by treating cooking as a cultural and artistic practic
 e. From April to July 2027 the selected resident develops an original proj
 ect at the intersection of art\, food and society and presents it as part 
 of the museum's public programme\, opening up new perspectives on art\, fo
 od and social questions and actively engaging visitors. The residency give
 s space to develop new formats and culinary projects across art\, cooking\
 , food\, culture\, sustainability and social issues\, with the museum unde
 rstood as a place of exchange and encounter. ELIGIBILITY: chefs\, artists\
 , food designers and interdisciplinary practitioners whose work engages qu
 estions of community\, memory\, hospitality\, ecology and the future of ea
 ting\; applicants from diverse backgrounds and perspectives are explicitly
  encouraged. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,000 per month\, furnished apartment\, travel 
 reimbursement to the start of the residency\, a Deutschlandticket\, possib
 le coverage of production costs\, museum access and team support. APPLICAT
 ION: a single PDF (max 10 pages\, 5 MB) with a short biography\, portfolio
  or work samples\, a project description (max 2 pages) and a cost estimate
  (max 1 page)\, emailed to residency@dasminsk.de. DEADLINE: 5 September 20
 26\, 11:59pm. Results expected November or December 2026. No fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: DAS MINSK Kunsthaus in Potsdam\nLocation: Potsdam\, Germany (Max-
 Planck-Strasse 17\, 14473 Potsdam). In-person residency at the museum\; op
 en internationally.\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,000 per month for four month
 s (EUR 4\,000 total)\, plus a furnished apartment (accommodation for up to
  three people\, so family can join\, though their travel and living costs 
 are not covered)\, reimbursement of travel expenses to the start of the re
 sidency\, a Deutschlandticket for the duration\, and the possibility of pr
 oduction costs for the proposed project being covered. Access to the museu
 m's exhibitions and relevant work areas\, and support from the museum team
 . One residency awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Four months\, Apri
 l to July 2027\n\nMore: https://dasminsk.de/en/residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dasminsk.de/en/residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Potsdam\, Germany (Max-Planck-Strasse 17\, 14473 Potsdam). In-pers
 on residency at the museum\; open internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldrausch-kuenstlerinnenprojekt-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Goldrausch Kuenstlerinnenprojekt 2027 (FLINTA Professiona
 l Development Programme)
DESCRIPTION:Run since 1989 by Goldrausch Frauennetzwerk e. V. to counteract
  the structural discrimination faced by FLINTA artists\, the Goldrausch Ku
 enstlerinnenprojekt is a year-long professional development programme for 
 15 Berlin-based visual artists. The participants' own artistic practice is
  the starting point: weekly courses on two fixed days\, individual appoint
 ments and three to four intensive weeks combine practice-oriented learning
  with insight into how the art world works\, plus continuous training in p
 resentation skills and communication strategy. The curriculum covers the d
 esign of an individual artist website\, studio talks and group critiques\,
  the fundamentals of self-employment\, public relations and project planni
 ng\, and culminates in a published catalogue and a group exhibition in the
  autumn. Seminars are led by art historians and cultural scholars\, with c
 urators\, gallerists and other arts professionals invited for peer-to-peer
  exchange. The alumnae network now runs to more than 525 graduates. ELIGIB
 ILITY: FLINTA visual artists of any age working in any field\, preferably 
 with a fine arts degree or equivalent experience\; must be based in Berlin
 \; German and English sufficient to follow group discussion is required\; 
 an active practice with clear goals and the capacity to devote time to com
 munication work alongside studio practice. APPLICATION: a written applicat
 ion in German or English\, submitted via the open call documents on the Go
 ldrausch site. A two-stage external jury of experts first shortlists on th
 e written applications\, then selects the 15 participants through small gr
 oup interviews. Selection criteria are the quality of the artistic work an
 d how meaningfully the programme complements the applicant's professional 
 practice. DEADLINE: 15 September 2026. No fee.\n\nOrganisation: Goldrausch
  Frauennetzwerk e. V.\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Applicants must be base
 d in Berlin and able to attend in person on two fixed weekdays plus three 
 to four intensive weeks across the year.\nAward: Fully funded twelve-month
  professional development programme\, co-funded by the European Union (Eur
 opean Social Fund Plus) and the Federal State of Berlin\, so participants 
 pay nothing: there is no course fee and no application fee. 15 places are 
 awarded per year. The programme covers the production of a printed catalog
 ue\, a group exhibition\, an individually designed artist website\, weekly
  seminars\, and one-to-one appointments with art historians\, curators and
  gallerists. No cash stipend or production budget is paid to participants.
 \nDuration: 12 months\, January to December 2027\n\nMore: https://goldraus
 ch.org/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://goldrausch.org/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Applicants must be based in Berlin and able to a
 ttend in person on two fixed weekdays plus three to four intensive weeks a
 cross the year.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:darc-transmediale-interstices-research-workshop-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x DARC: Interstices\, Research (in) the Gaps
 \, PhD/Research Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The annual DARC PhD/Research Workshop\, organised by the Digita
 l Aesthetics Research Center at Aarhus University with transmediale\, resp
 onds to transmediale's 2027 thematic framework. THEME: 'Interstices: Resea
 rch (in) the gaps'. An interstice is the small space between objects set c
 losely together\, the cords in a rope or the atoms in a crystal lattice: a
 n emptiness produced by the structure it belongs to\, and without which th
 at structure could not be what it is. In crystallography\, interstitial si
 tes are the spaces a lattice and its basis generate but do not fill\, and 
 interstitial diffusion\, the movement of small atoms through the gaps of a
  host lattice\, is the mechanism by which materials transform. The call as
 ks what the equivalent sites are in social\, cultural and computational st
 ructures: where are the gaps these combinations generate but do not fill\,
  what moves through them\, and do they carry transformative power? It work
 s through Yancey Strickler's dark forest theory of the internet (the withd
 rawal of meaningful exchange from the open\, surveilled\, indexed web into
  private channels)\, the Dark Forest Collective's anthology and its 'cozyw
 eb' of small sheltered spaces\, dark nets\, miniverses and moving castles 
 as interstitial spaces produced by and defined against the dominant web\, 
 and Bogna Konior's extension of the dark forest metaphor to the opacity of
  AI systems\, where silence is refusal rather than absence and the forest 
 is increasingly inhabited by other-than-human intelligences that opt out o
 f engagement with people. Where big tech pursues efficiency through the au
 tomation of human perception\, cognition\, identification and aesthetics\,
  artists and researchers explore the non/more-than-human\, glitchy\, noisy
 \, machinic\, datafied and dark to build new expression and critique of da
 ta-ism and what is marketed as artificial intelligence\, including the dan
 gers and potentials inside badly curated data models\, between polluting d
 ata centres\, and in skeuomorphic interfaces. WHAT THEY WANT: proposals fr
 om artists\, researchers and practitioners for work that occupies and move
 s through gaps that are social as well as structural\, ontological and mat
 erial. The gaps are physical too: the heat of data centres and their thirs
 t for water\, latency in the cables\, unindexed nodes. The call invites sp
 eculations\, practical interventions and inferences that fill the gaps and
  expand the diversity of possible communications and communities that can 
 inhabit dark forests\, including those built on\, against and beneath the 
 infrastructures underlying them\, and welcomes work on the (dis-)continuou
 s histories of technological exploration of computational infrastructures 
 over the last 30 years or longer\, and on how current artistic\, theoretic
 al and technical explorations repeat or break from them. WHO: PhD candidat
 es and early-career researchers\, with submissions welcome from researcher
 s inside and outside the academy\, including artists\, designers and curat
 ors. PARTICIPANT EXPECTATIONS: participants write a paper and present it a
 t the workshop\, and on the basis of that peer review shorten the research
  into a newspaper-length article for distribution at the transmediale fest
 ival. The workshop is led by scholars from DARC at Aarhus University. DEAD
 LINE: 28 August 2026\, 23:59 CEST\, via the application link on the call p
 age. Queries to Pablo Velasco\, pvelasco[at]cc.au.dk.\n\nOrganisation: Dig
 ital Aesthetics Research Center (DARC)\, Aarhus University\, in collaborat
 ion with transmediale\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\; the workshop runs alon
 gside transmediale 2027 (festival 26 to 31 January 2027). Open to research
 ers based anywhere\, inside or outside the academy.\nAward: No submission 
 fee. The published call does not state a participation fee\, honorarium\, 
 travel or accommodation support\, so confirm with the organisers before bu
 dgeting. Accepted participants present a paper at the workshop and their c
 ondensed text is distributed as a newspaper-style article at the festival.
 \nDuration: Research workshop held around transmediale 2027 in Berlin (fes
 tival 26 to 31 January 2027)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/open
 -call-for-darc-phd-research-workshop-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/open-call-for-darc-phd-research-worksho
 p-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\; the workshop runs alongside transmediale 2027 (
 festival 26 to 31 January 2027). Open to researchers based anywhere\, insi
 de or outside the academy.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iclc-2027-antwerp-call-for-participation@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: ICLC 2027: International Conference on Live Coding\, Call
  for Participation (Dialogues)
DESCRIPTION:The International Conference on Live Coding is dedicated to pra
 ctices and research focused on technologies and philosophies that interpre
 t the use of computer code and the public writing of algorithms as perform
 ative gestures. The 10th edition runs 9 to 13 March 2027 in Antwerp\, host
 ed by Lambdasonic (TOPLAP Belgium) with the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp
  and De Singel. THEME: 'Dialogues'\, framing live coding as continuous imp
 rovisational exchange between coder\, machine and audience\, and across di
 sciplines. Suggested topics include dialogues between live coding and acou
 stic musicians\, dancers\, theatre\, classically trained musicians reading
  live-coded (or graphical) scores\, band and jazz-combo settings\, live-co
 der ensembles\, ten-minute live-coded mini-operas\, DMX lighting systems\,
  graphics and shader live coding\, robotics (pen plotters\, textile-weavin
 g robots)\, design-as-performance\, community building\, diversity/equity/
 inclusion\, accessibility of live coding languages and interfaces\, educat
 ion\, and algorave. The venues will facilitate collaborations with residen
 t dancers\, a jazz combo (back-line provided: drums\, guitar amp\, bass am
 p\, piano)\, a string quartet reading scores a prima vista\, visual artist
 s\, students and researchers where possible. FORMATS: short papers (2-4 pa
 ges) and long papers (5-12 pages) using the provided template\; live perfo
 rmances (800-word abstract\, max 150-word programme note\, technical rider
 )\; workshops (short 2h or long 4h\, max 700-word abstract\, held in Engli
 sh or Dutch)\; installations (max 700-word abstract\, technical questionna
 ire plus a measured plan or sketch\, with the interactive aspect clearly d
 efined)\; and satellite events. All contributors submit a max 150-word bio
 graphy. Peer review is single-blind with at least two reviewers per submis
 sion. LANGUAGE: submissions must be in English\, except that live performa
 nce\, installation and workshop proposals may also be submitted in another
  language (workshops: English\, Dutch or French) with a machine-translated
  English version\, stated as such. Substantial use of generative AI in wri
 ting papers and performance abstracts must be disclosed\; proofreading and
  translation are exempt. In-person presentation is encouraged\, with remot
 e proposals considered and sessions live-streamed where possible\; the org
 anisers ask attendees to minimise travel impact and to link up with nearby
  satellite events to turn a long trip into a mini-tour. The call notes att
 ention to access needs\, care responsibilities and other barriers to parti
 cipation. SATELLITE EVENTS: live coding nodes\, art schools and other orga
 nisations worldwide are invited to host their own events before or after I
 CLC 2027\; submit a declaration of interest via Fourwaves before 1 Februar
 y 2027 with a principal contact\, city and any confirmed details\, and joi
 n #iclc-satellite-events on the TOPLAP Discord. Hosts are asked to seek lo
 cal funding for accommodation\, travel and artist fees\; the committee can
 not fund or organise these but will coordinate dates and publish your even
 t. TO APPLY: submit via Fourwaves at https://event.fourwaves.com/iclc2027/
 pages using the templates at https://codeberg.org/iclc/iclc-templates (rea
 d the README for full proposal instructions). Submission deadline extended
  to 1 September 2026\; acceptance notification 1 November 2026. CALL FOR R
 EVIEWERS: anyone active in a live-coding-related field can volunteer by em
 ailing a short description and keywords of their expertise to iclc@lambdas
 onic.be\, the same address for general questions.\n\nOrganisation: Lambdas
 onic (TOPLAP Belgium)\, Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp and De Singel\nLoca
 tion: Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp and De Singel International Arts Cent
 er\, Antwerp\, Belgium. Open to anyone engaged with live coding\; remote p
 articipation considered.\nAward: NO submission fee. The call does not stat
 e artist fees\, travel support or accommodation for accepted contributors\
 , so budget for self-funded attendance unless the organisers announce othe
 rwise. Proceedings are published with a DOI per article. Satellite-event h
 osts can request a Letter of Intent to support their own local funding app
 lications.\nDuration: Five-day conference\, 9 to 13 March 2027. Workshops 
 are 2 hours (short) or 4 hours (long).\n\nMore: https://iclc.toplap.org/20
 27/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iclc.toplap.org/2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp and De Singel International Arts Ce
 nter\, Antwerp\, Belgium. Open to anyone engaged with live coding\; remote
  participation considered.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-voucher-art-event-mexico-art-week-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Voucher Art Event\, Mexico Art Week 2027
DESCRIPTION:A Mondriaan Fund voucher sending visual artists to Mexico Art W
 eek 2027 in Mexico City\, built around the Zona Maco art fair. The voucher
  covers admission to the Zona Maco preview days\, a curated programme duri
 ng the week\, a networking event with the Dutch Embassy and hotel accommod
 ation from 2 to 7 February 2027\, plus a EUR 1\,300 contribution to travel
  costs. Fifteen vouchers are available. ELIGIBILITY: visual artists from t
 he Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom with at least one year
  of professional practice. Applicants may not be enrolled in a bachelor's\
 , master's or PhD programme\, with an exception for part-time programmes u
 nder 20 hours per week. CONDITIONS: the artist must be available to stay i
 n Mexico City from 2 to 7 February 2027 and take part in all scheduled act
 ivities\, and must submit a written evaluation after the visit. APPLY thro
 ugh the Mondriaan Fund online system with a CV (maximum three pages)\, a m
 otivation statement addressing your international ambitions\, the relevanc
 e of Mexico Art Week to your practice and your networking strategy\, bank 
 details and\, if applicable\, a BRP extract. Deadline 10 September 2026 be
 fore 16:00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan F
 und\nLocation: Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbea
 n part of the Kingdom. The event takes place in Mexico City\, Mexico.\nAwa
 rd: A voucher covering admission to the Zona Maco preview days\, a curated
  programme during Mexico Art Week 2027\, a networking event with the Dutch
  Embassy\, and hotel accommodation from 2 to 7 February 2027\, plus a EUR 
 1\,300 contribution towards travel costs. 15 vouchers are available. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Mexico Art Week 2027 runs 3 to 7 February 2027\;
  the artist must be available to stay in Mexico City from 2 to 7 February 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/v
 oucher-art-event-mexico-art-week-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/voucher-art-e
 vent-mexico-art-week-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom. The event takes place in Mexico City\, Mexico.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-international-collaborative-projects-heritage-institutes-2026
 @artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: International Collaborative Projects with
  Heritage Institutes (September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This scheme funds cultural heritage institutions in the Netherl
 ands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom that want to collaborate with f
 oreign heritage institutions on research projects in shared collection are
 as\, including art historical and provenance research. A development phase
  can also be funded\, covering travel\, accommodation and presentation cos
 ts while the collaboration is being shaped. CONDITIONS: the applicant inst
 itution must be publicly accessible and manage nationally significant cult
 ural heritage\; it must partner with comparable institutions abroad\; the 
 research must be presented by both the Dutch and the international partner
 s\; the applicant must contribute significantly to financing the project\;
  and the international partners' share of costs must be proportional to th
 e Mondriaan Fund grant. AMOUNTS: up to 40% of variable project costs for t
 he main project\, or up to 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000 for
  development research. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund online application
  system after registering an account. Deadline 10 September 2026 before 16
 :00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time (an earlier 28 May 2026 round has pa
 ssed).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Applicant institutions m
 ust be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; the
  partner institutions are abroad.\nAward: Determined per application. Up t
 o 40% of variable project costs. For a development research phase\, up to 
 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000\, covering travel\, accommodat
 ion and presentation costs. The applicant must contribute significantly to
  the project financing\, and the international partners' cost share must b
 e proportional to the Mondriaan Fund grant. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Project-based research collaboration. Two annual rounds\; this card cover
 s the 10 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/e
 n/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international-collaborative-projects-with-herit
 age-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international
 -collaborative-projects-with-heritage-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant institutions must be based in the Netherlands or the Car
 ibbean part of the Kingdom\; the partner institutions are abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-heritage-innovation-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Heritage Innovation (September 2026 round
 )
DESCRIPTION:Heritage Innovation funds projects and research tracks that con
 tribute to substantive innovation in the heritage sector. Examples given b
 y the fund include developing new narratives about cultural heritage\, str
 engthening regional collaboration across the sector\, redesigning how a co
 llection is presented\, and feasibility studies on technological applicati
 ons such as AI or gamification\, which makes this one of the more tech-adj
 acent Mondriaan schemes. WHO CAN APPLY: museums and collection-holding cul
 tural heritage institutions\, including archives\, in the Netherlands and 
 the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. Cultural organisations in the heritage 
 sector may also apply if they collaborate with one or more collection-hold
 ing institutions. All applicants must be non-profit\, not-for-profit entit
 ies. NOT FUNDED: fixed costs\, restoration\, building museums\, or regular
  operations. CONDITIONS: institutions must subscribe to the Fair Practice 
 Code\, the Culture Governance Code and the Diversity and Inclusion Code\, 
 and must pay visual artists fairly where artists are involved. AMOUNTS: pr
 ojects get up to 40% of variable project-related costs on a minimum projec
 t budget of EUR 25\,000\; research tracks get up to 70% of costs capped at
  EUR 15\,000 with no minimum budget. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund onli
 ne system after registering an account. Deadline 17 September 2026 before 
 16:00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\n
 Location: Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Neth
 erlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.\nAward: Projects: up to 40%
  of variable project-related costs\, with a minimum project budget of EUR 
 25\,000. Research tracks: up to 70% of costs\, capped at EUR 15\,000\, wit
 h no minimum budget. No application fee.\nDuration: Project or research tr
 ack. This card covers the 17 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www
 .mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-innovation/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-inno
 vation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Nether
 lands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-biologica-artxscience-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ars Biologica ArtXScience Residency 2027-2028 (Ars Electr
 onica x Ceske Budejovice ECoC 2028)
DESCRIPTION:A fully funded art-science residency from Ars Electronica and C
 eske Budejovice\, European Capital of Culture 2028\, exploring how art and
  science can collaborate on urgent environmental challenges: climate emerg
 ence\, sustainable agriculture\, geoengineering\, permaculture\, water res
 ource management\, and the broader ecological impacts on local communities
 . Selected residents work in direct collaboration with local scientists in
  Ceske Budejovice. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, creatives and arti
 st collectives with more than 5 years of professional creative practice an
 d documented interdisciplinary work\; experience in community engagement a
 nd science collaborations is essential\; applicants must be 18+\, of any n
 ationality\, and legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. WHAT YOU G
 ET: a EUR 24\,000 package (EUR 6\,000 artist fee\, up to EUR 15\,000 produ
 ction\, up to EUR 3\,000 travel and subsistence) plus one month of housing
  covered separately\; two winners are selected. STRUCTURE: the residency r
 uns January 2027 to April 2028\, with a required on-site stay of up to one
  month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/September 2027\
 , and a March 2028 stay for festival installation\, exhibition and deinsta
 llation. HOW TO APPLY: online form with project title\, a written proposal
  of max 250 words\, a scientific direction statement (max 100 words)\, art
 istic vision (max 100 words)\, community connection plan (max 100 words)\,
  a super short pitch (3 to 30 words)\, 3 to 7 images\, an optional 1-minut
 e video\, a portfolio link and contact information. Two-round selection (o
 nline application then interview)\; winners notified by November 2026. Dea
 dline 28 September 2026 at midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica 
 and Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Ceske B
 udejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any nationality aged 18+
  who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Required on-site s
 tays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/
 September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibition and deinstal
 lation.\nAward: EUR 24\,000 total package per winner: EUR 6\,000 artist fe
 e\, up to EUR 15\,000 production budget\, and up to EUR 3\,000 for travel\
 , accommodation and subsistence\, plus a separate budget covering one mont
 h of housing in Ceske Budejovice. Two positions available. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: January 2027 to April 2028\, with on-site blocks in early 2027 
 and March 2028\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars
 -biologica-art-science-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars-biologica-art-scienc
 e-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ceske Budejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any natio
 nality aged 18+ who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Req
 uired on-site stays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional 
 stay in August/September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibiti
 on and deinstallation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:knowcase-sonar-cotec-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: KNOWCASE Open Call 2027: permanent digital-culture instal
 lation in Madrid (Sonar+D x Fundacion Cotec)
DESCRIPTION:Fundacion Cotec (a Spanish innovation-focused non-profit) and S
 onar+D\, building on an initial experiment at Sonar 2026\, invite proposal
 s for a long-term installation at KNOWCASE\, the street-level showcase of 
 Cotec's Madrid headquarters in Chamberi\, visible to the public 24 hours a
  day. THEME: digital culture\, meaning projects that combine knowledge\, r
 esearch\, science and data with art\, technology and social impact. Cotec'
 s stated priorities are the big transitions (analogue to digital\, linear 
 to circular economy\, tangible to intangible) plus innovation ecosystems a
 nd R&D&I\, the climate crisis\, the future of work and learning\, social d
 ivides\, citizen participation and democratic health. WHAT YOU GET: a budg
 et of up to EUR 100\,000 plus VAT covering everything (design\, production
 \, installation\, maintenance\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, acc
 ommodation and insurance)\, and a minimum 24-month public display from Feb
 ruary 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, collectives\, designers\, technologis
 ts\, universities\, research centres\, startups\, businesses\, creative ag
 encies\, producers\, cultural institutions and multidisciplinary teams\, i
 nternationally\; applicants must demonstrate solid experience and a releva
 nt portfolio. CONSTRAINTS: the proposal must be original and never previou
 sly exhibited\, must include participative or interactive elements\, must 
 encourage critical thinking\, and must be technically and financially viab
 le for the full 24+ month exhibition period (durability and maintenance ar
 e central selection criteria). Selection weighs conceptual quality highest
  (40 percent)\, followed by public interactivity (25 percent). HOW TO APPL
 Y: one PDF of maximum 15 pages containing summary\, concept\, technical pr
 oposal\, visuals\, budget\, timeline\, team profile\, portfolio and declar
 ation\, in Spanish\, another official language of Spain\, or English\, via
  the application portal linked from the terms and conditions. Results anno
 unced 14 October 2026. Deadline 7 September 2026 at midnight CEST.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Fundacion Cotec and Sonar+D\nLocation: Installation at the KNOWC
 ASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headquarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Sp
 ain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. The call is international\; appli
 cations accepted in Spanish\, other official languages of Spain\, or Engli
 sh.\nAward: Up to EUR 100\,000 (plus VAT)\, all-inclusive: conceptualisati
 on\, design\, technical development\, production\, installation\, maintena
 nce\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, accommodation and insurance.\
 nDuration: Installation displayed for a minimum of 24 months\, starting Fe
 bruary 2027\n\nMore: https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Installation at the KNOWCASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headq
 uarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Spain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. 
 The call is international\; applications accepted in Spanish\, other offic
 ial languages of Spain\, or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:studio-alta-residence-2027-open-calls@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Studio ALTA Residence 2027: four residency open calls (Pr
 ague)
DESCRIPTION:Prague performance venue Studio ALTA announces four residency o
 pen calls for 2027\, all with a single deadline of 10 September 2026. RESE
 ARCH HOUSE (19 to 28 April 2027): a shared residential laboratory for thre
 e art projects or individual artists in the early stages of exploration an
 d experimentation\, or reopening an existing finished work (performance\, 
 installation\, object\, video) to transform it into another form such as a
  workshop\, text or performance-lecture. Includes a 10-day residency\, a f
 ee of CZK 12\,000 per project\, shared studio\, individual workspace and f
 acilitated exchange meetings\; the research output must be shared publicly
  as a work-in-progress in a form based on participants' needs. REST HOUSE 
 (March to November 2027): a five-day residential spa for overloaded collea
 gues from the arts sector\, with no required output or activities\; restri
 cted to people working in production\, dramaturgy\, curation\, PR\, techni
 cal and other supporting artistic professions in the Czech independent sec
 tor. Two guests are chosen by lottery (fee CZK 6\,000 per person)\; the pu
 blic draw is announced 16 September 2026. HOUSE IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD (9 to 
 18 August 2027): for one performative art project created with the local c
 ommunity and designed or adapted for public space in Liben and its surroun
 dings\; this year's call focuses on the 55+ target group. Includes a fee o
 f CZK 30\,000 per project\, rehearsal and indoor facilities (primarily out
 door spaces)\, dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, 
 connections to partner organisations\, and 7 days of intensive production 
 and technical support in the final phase. A public premiere or work-in-pro
 gress in public space at the end of the residency is required. HOUSE OF SW
 EAT (1 to 10 February 2027): for one performative art project designed or 
 adapted for the specific environment of the Studio ALTA sauna and its imme
 diate surroundings\, seeking new ways of working with intimate space\, pro
 ximity to the audience and non-traditional formats. Includes a fee of CZK 
 15\,000 per project\, a 10-day residency\, sauna and rehearsal spaces\, dr
 amaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, and 2 days of int
 ensive final-phase support\; a public work-in-progress or premiere in the 
 sauna within the 9 to 12 February 2027 programme block is required. Projec
 ts at any stage of development can apply to the production calls\, and sel
 ected projects may be included in Studio ALTA's year-round programme. TIME
 LINE: deadline 10 September 2026\; results 3 weeks after the deadline (30 
 September 2026)\; a Q&A Zoom call takes place 10 August 2026 at 3:00 PM. A
 pply via the registration forms on the call page.\n\nOrganisation: Studio 
 ALTA\nLocation: Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Th
 ree of the four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is re
 served for supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independ
 ent sector.\nAward: Residency fees paid to participants: Research House CZ
 K 12\,000 per project\; Rest House CZK 6\,000 per person\; House in the Ne
 ighborhood CZK 30\,000 per project\; House of Sweat CZK 15\,000 per projec
 t. All include workspace at Studio ALTA\; the two production residencies a
 dd dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR support. Free to apply.\nDu
 ration: Programme dependent: 5 to 10 days\, at various points between Febr
 uary and November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Three of t
 he four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is reserved f
 or supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independent sect
 or.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fucina-futura-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fucina Futura 2027 Residency (Marostica\, Italy)
DESCRIPTION:Fucina Futura is an artist residency in Marostica\, a small tow
 n about an hour from Venice\, offering a peaceful setting to develop resea
 rch in close contact with nature and the local community. The project span
 s two locations: the home designed by internationally renowned illustrator
  Elena Xausa near the historic centre\, and the atelier Fucina Ai Gorghi b
 y beloved local painter Daniele Marcon\, ideal for large-scale installatio
 ns. Led by visual artist Lavinia and curator Sofia (Futura Association)\, 
 the program invites residents to develop projects that engage with the com
 munity and the working location\, and encourages artists of any discipline
  to make full use of the large atelier. The central goal is the 'restituti
 on' to citizens\, fostering cultural exchange and community inclusion: thi
 s final phase is tailored to each artist and can take the form of an exhib
 ition\, performance\, workshop\, screening\, talk or informal sharing sess
 ion\, prioritising direct dialogue with the public and the contemporary re
 newal of local tradition. THREE residents are hosted together from 12 Apri
 l to 12 May 2027 and share a spacious house\; they receive a daily fee to 
 cover living expenses\, and travel expenses are also covered. Made possibl
 e by Culture Moves Europe. ELIGIBILITY: only artists residing in one of th
 e Creative Europe countries EXCEPT ITALY may apply. Creative Europe covers
  the 27 EU member states (other than Italy)\, plus Albania\, Armenia\, Bos
 nia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Liechtenstein\, Moldova
 \, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, Tunisia and Ukraine\, 
 and includes the EU's Overseas Countries and Territories and Outermost Reg
 ions (Greenland\; French Guiana\, French Polynesia\, French Southern and A
 ntarctic Territories\, Guadeloupe\, Martinique\, Mayotte\, New Caledonia\,
  Reunion\, Saint Barthelemy\, Saint-Martin\, St. Pierre and Miquelon\, Wal
 lis and Futuna\; Azores\, Madeira\; Canary Islands\; Aruba\, Bonaire\, Cur
 acao\, Saba\, Sint Maarten\, Sint Eustatius). TIMELINE: apply via the Goog
 le Form by 20 August 2026\; selected artists informed by 30 August and mus
 t confirm participation by 8 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Futura Assoc
 iation (Fucina Futura)\, supported by Culture Moves Europe\nLocation: Maro
 stica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident in a Creati
 ve Europe country except Italy.\nAward: Fully funded: daily fee to cover l
 iving expenses\, travel costs covered\, and shared house accommodation pro
 vided (supported by Culture Moves Europe). No application fee.\nDuration: 
 One month\, 12 April to 12 May 2027\; three residents hosted together\n\nM
 ore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGr
 iMX0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGriM
 X0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Marostica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident
  in a Creative Europe country except Italy.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ace-pice-visitantes-2026-fase3@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Accion Cultural Espanola: PICE Visitantes 2026 (Phase 3)
DESCRIPTION:PICE Visitantes is the inbound mirror of PICE Movilidad: a Span
 ish festival\, biennial\, fair\, museum or platform applies for AC/E to fu
 nd bringing international programmers\, curators\, producers and cultural 
 professionals to its event in Spain\, so that they meet Spanish artists an
 d go on to programme them abroad. It is direct money to an organisation to
  enrich a festival or public programme it is already hosting. The same ten
  thematic areas apply as in Movilidad\, including Artes visuales\, Musica 
 y creacion sonora\, Podcast and Videojuego y animacion\, giving good cover
 age for media-arts\, sound-art and creative-technology events. Covered cos
 ts are travel\, accommodation\, travel insurance\, internal transport\, te
 xt translation and simultaneous or consecutive interpretation for the invi
 ted visitors\, with the exact list varying slightly by thematic area. Only
  entities constituted in Spain may apply\; natural persons are barred. Inv
 ited guests may come from any country including non-EU and the UK. TIMING:
  Phase 3 closes 7 September 2026\, provisional list 21 October\, definitiv
 e list 30 October\, and visits may not start before 1 November 2026. Appli
 cations go through the AC/E PICE online system in Spanish or English with 
 no fee.\n\nOrganisation: Accion Cultural Espanola (AC/E)\nLocation: Spain.
  The host event must take place in Spain and the applicant must be constit
 uted in Spain.\nAward: Max EUR 20\,000 per applicant per call\, per event 
 and per thematic area\; within that\, max EUR 2\,000 per international vis
 itor. Total 2026 call budget EUR 1\,200\,000 (Cine EUR 180\,000\, Artes vi
 suales EUR 160\,000\, Musica y creacion sonora EUR 150\,000\, Literatura E
 UR 150\,000\, Arquitectura y diseno EUR 90\,000\, Podcast EUR 90\,000\, Vi
 deojuego y animacion EUR 90\,000). No application fee.\nDuration: Single e
 vent\; Phase 3 visits must start on or after 1 November 2026 and finish be
 fore 28 February 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.accioncultural.es/es/visitante
 s-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.accioncultural.es/es/visitantes-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Spain. The host event must take place in Spain and the applicant m
 ust be constituted in Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-crt-orizzonti-live-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione CRT: Orizzonti L.I.V.E. 2026 (second session)
DESCRIPTION:Orizzonti L.I.V.E. is Fondazione CRT's flagship thematic call f
 or organisations that programme live performance as a driver of territoria
 l transformation. The acronym stands for Luoghi\, Impatto\, Visioni\, Ener
 gia\, and stated priorities are strengthening organisations rooted in thei
 r territory\, audience development reaching new publics\, social inclusion
  and access for economically or socially fragile audiences\, professional 
 engagement of young musicians\, actors and dancers\, audience engagement a
 imed at under-25s\, stable networks and strategic partnerships\, and envir
 onmental sustainability aligned with Agenda 2030. This is festival and sea
 son funding at meaningful scale: the maximum request is EUR 100\,000 and t
 he overall project budget must itself be at least EUR 100\,000\, with co-f
 inancing covering at least 70 percent of eligible costs\, so the applicant
  must bring roughly EUR 70\,000 from other sources. The 2026 call runs in 
 two sessions: the first closed 27 February 2026\, and the second closes 15
  September 2026 at 15:00 Italian time. Applications go through rol.fondazi
 onecrt.it. SCOPE CAVEAT: this is broad live-performance funding rather tha
 n a media-arts line\, so it fits experimental performance\, sound art and 
 hybrid live work but also covers conventional music and theatre. Non-EU an
 d UK organisations can realistically only participate as project partners\
 , not as lead applicants.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione CRT (Fondazione Cass
 a di Risparmio di Torino)\nLocation: Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. A
 ctivities must be delivered in those regions\; the applicant does not itse
 lf have to be headquartered there.\nAward: Max EUR 100\,000 requestable. T
 he project's own budget must be at least EUR 100\,000. Mandatory co-financ
 ing of at least 70 percent of eligible project costs\, so CRT covers a max
 imum of 30 percent. The requested amount is assessed against the applicant
 's last approved annual accounts and grant history. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Project period set in the application\; extensions of the grant-u
 se deadline of up to 12 months may be requested.\n\nMore: https://www.fond
 azionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/orizzonti-l-i-v-e/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/orizzonti-l-i-v-e/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. Activities must be delivered i
 n those regions\; the applicant does not itself have to be headquartered t
 here.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturdirektoratet-tverrfaglig-kulturvirksomhet-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturdirektoratet: Cross-Disciplinary Cultural Activity\
 , Events\, Organisers and Venues (2026 autumn round)
DESCRIPTION:Kulturdirektoratet's main scheme for multi-artistic and cross-d
 isciplinary events\, organisers and venues\, and the natural Norwegian rou
 te for a festival or biennial that does not sit inside a single artform co
 mmittee. It funds single events\, event series\, festivals and seminars wi
 th cross-disciplinary relevance\, plus year-round operation of organisatio
 ns with a multi-artistic profile\, which covers media arts\, digital cultu
 re and experimental sound programming presented alongside other forms. Art
  production itself\, closed workshops\, infrastructure investment and acti
 vity already completed before the deadline are not funded. Two application
  rounds run in 2026: 8 April 2026 (project grants\, closed) and 15 Septemb
 er 2026 at 13:00 (project grants plus activity grants for the 2027 operati
 ng year). Project grants accept individuals\, private and public instituti
 ons\, and organisations\, while activity grants require an organisation nu
 mber or a named\, separately budgeted activity within a larger entity\, ex
 isting for at least one year and not already receiving permanent annual st
 ate funding. The scheme never fully finances a project\, so a credible co-
 financing plan is expected. FLAG: decision dates and foreign-applicant eli
 gibility are not published on the scheme page\; award notifications arrive
  via the application portal.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturdirektoratet (Arts and
  Culture Norway)\nLocation: Norway. Activity is expected to take place in 
 Norway\, though international artists and partners can be programmed.\nAwa
 rd: NOK. No fixed minimum or maximum published\; grant sizes are assessed 
 against the project budget\, financing plan and available funds. Kulturdir
 ektoratet states it does not provide full financing\, so co-financing is r
 equired in practice but no fixed percentage is set. Historical award level
 s are published in the scheme's public decision database. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Project grants for single events or series\; activity grant
 s cover the 2027 operating year.\n\nMore: https://www.kulturdirektoratet.n
 o/tilskuddsordninger/tverrfaglig-kulturvirksomhet-arrangementer-arrangoere
 r-og-arenaer?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturdirektoratet.no/tilskuddsordninger/tverrfaglig-kultur
 virksomhet-arrangementer-arrangoerer-og-arenaer?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Norway. Activity is expected to take place in Norway\, though inte
 rnational artists and partners can be programmed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturdirektoratet-arrangoerstoette-visuell-kunst-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturdirektoratet: Arrangorstotte Visuell Kunst\, Visual
  Art Organisers Support (2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This scheme gives operating and programme support to visual art
  organisers in Norway\, covering exhibition and event programming\, conten
 t production\, salaries\, artist fees\, venue costs including rent\, utili
 ties and internet\, and administrative expenses. Because it funds the orga
 niser rather than a single artwork\, it is the relevant route for an artis
 t-run space\, biennial organisation or media-arts venue running a recurrin
 g public programme. Applicants must demonstrate artistic and cultural expe
 rtise\, innovation and distinctiveness. Eligibility is limited to bodies w
 ith their own registration number\, or a separately named and budgeted act
 ivity within a larger organisation\, existing for at least one year prior 
 to application\, and organisations already receiving permanent annual stat
 e funding are excluded. The 2026 application deadline is 15 September 2026
  at 13:00. Kulturdirektoratet explicitly warns that applicants often recei
 ve less than requested or are rejected despite quality proposals\, so co-f
 inancing is necessary. FLAG: amounts\, decision lag and foreign-applicant 
 eligibility are not published on the funder's page\; results arrive throug
 h the application portal with an acceptance deadline in the decision lette
 r.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturdirektoratet (Arts and Culture Norway)\nLocation
 : Norway. Foreign applicant eligibility is not stated on the scheme page.\
 nAward: NOK. No published minimum or maximum\; award sizes vary with budge
 t and available funds and previous awards are listed in the scheme's decis
 ion database. Kulturdirektoratet does not provide full financing\, so co-f
 inancing is expected and applicants often receive less than requested. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Operating and programme support\, typically co
 vering the following activity year.\n\nMore: https://www.kulturdirektorate
 t.no/tilskuddsordninger/arrangoerstoette-visuell-kunst?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturdirektoratet.no/tilskuddsordninger/arrangoerstoette-v
 isuell-kunst?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Norway. Foreign applicant eligibility is not stated on the scheme 
 page.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:statens-kunstfond-production-exhibitions-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Statens Kunstfond: Production and Exhibitions\, Contempor
 ary Art in Denmark and Abroad (2026 autumn round)
DESCRIPTION:The Danish Arts Foundation's Production and Exhibitions program
 me funds the production\, dissemination and exhibition of contemporary art
  in Denmark and abroad\, and it is one of the few Nordic national schemes 
 a foreign organisation can apply to directly. Eligible costs include creat
 ing new works where an exhibition agreement is in place\, exhibition costs
 \, exhibition programming featuring Danish or international artists\, prom
 otion tied to an exhibition\, and honorariums covering artists' work and i
 nstallation time\, which lets a festival or biennial cover commission and 
 artist-fee lines. THE KEY CONDITION for non-Danish applicants is that the 
 exhibition must feature Danish artists\; Danish artists and venues face no
  such restriction. No minimum or maximum grant is published since the comm
 ittee decides case by case\, and previous award levels are visible on the 
 site. Two 2026 deadlines apply: 26 March 2026 (closed) and 24 September 20
 26 at 14:00\, with the application form opening one month before each dead
 line. TIMING: applicants receive a response no later than twelve weeks aft
 er the deadline\, so expect a decision by mid-December 2026. Applications 
 must go through the Danish digital subsidy portal\; submissions outside it
  are rejected except in very special circumstances. FLAG: earliest-start-d
 ate rules are not specified on the funder's page.\n\nOrganisation: Statens
  Kunstfond (Danish Arts Foundation)\nLocation: Denmark and abroad. Non-Dan
 ish venues and organisations may apply\, but only for exhibitions that fea
 ture Danish artists.\nAward: DKK. No published minimum or maximum\; the co
 mmittee assesses each application on its merits and historical awards are 
 published on the site. No stated co-financing requirement. No application 
 fee. Applications must be submitted digitally via the Danish subsidy porta
 l (Tilskudsportalen).\nDuration: Project-length\; production and exhibitio
 n periods vary.\n\nMore: https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/e
 xhibition-of-danish-art-abroad?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/exhibition-of-danish-ar
 t-abroad?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Denmark and abroad. Non-Danish venues and organisations may apply\
 , but only for exhibitions that feature Danish artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fonds-daku-global-village-kids-digital-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Darstellende Kuenste: GLOBAL VILLAGE KIDS im digita
 len Raum (2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The digital-space strand of the Fonds Darstellende Kuenste GLOB
 AL VILLAGE KIDS programme\, funding format-open and results-open artistic 
 projects and artist-participatory approaches in digital and hybrid perform
 ing arts. Eligible artistic fields explicitly include digital performing a
 rts alongside performance\, theatre\, dance\, musical theatre\, puppet the
 atre and contemporary circus\, which makes it usable for hybrid or online 
 public programmes. The applicant must be a coalition of at least three leg
 ally constituted organisations spanning arts and culture\, education and c
 ivil society\, all German-based\, so this is genuinely institution-facing 
 rather than artist-facing\; individual artists cannot apply\, and schools 
 and kindergartens may participate as partners but cannot be the applying o
 rganisation. Two tiers exist: laboratory projects at EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000
  requiring a minimum 30 hours of work\, and process projects at EUR 15\,00
 0 to 40\,000 requiring a minimum 60 hours\, both inclusive of a 7 percent 
 administrative fee. FULL FINANCING is available with no matching requireme
 nt\, which is unusual and valuable. TIMING: the deadline is 1 October 2026
  with the earliest permitted project start on 1 January 2027\, so the deci
 sion lag is roughly three months. Applications go exclusively through the 
 kumasta online database. FIT CAVEAT: the programme targets children and yo
 ung people aged 3 to 18 in situations of social\, financial or educational
  disadvantage\, so it suits a digital-arts programme with a youth particip
 ation core rather than a general public festival.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds D
 arstellende Kuenste e.V.\nLocation: Germany. All coalition members must be
  based in Germany\, though non-German artists may be involved as contracte
 d artists.\nAward: Laboratory projects EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000\; process pro
 jects EUR 15\,000 to 40\,000. Both figures include a 7 percent administrat
 ive overhead. Full financing model\, no co-financing required. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: Earliest start 1 January 2027\; projects must conclude
  by 31 August 2027\; final reports due 30 September 2027.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.fonds-daku.de/foerderung/foerderprogramme/global-village-kids-2/globa
 l-village-kids-im-digitalen-raum/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fonds-daku.de/foerderung/foerderprogramme/global-village-ki
 ds-2/global-village-kids-im-digitalen-raum/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany. All coalition members must be based in Germany\, though n
 on-German artists may be involved as contracted artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-crt-ordinarie-arte-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione CRT: Bando Ordinarie 2026\, Arte\, attivita e 
 beni culturali\, Progetti (second session)
DESCRIPTION:The Bando Ordinarie is Fondazione CRT's open\, non-thematic rou
 te: organisations can request support for initiatives that fit the foundat
 ion's statutory aims but do not fall under any of its thematic calls\, acr
 oss three areas of which one is Arte\, attivita e beni culturali (branded 
 Meraviglia). It is the right door for public programmes\, cultural project
 s\, media and digital-culture initiatives and events that are not live per
 formance\, exhibitions\, film festivals or restoration. READ THE EXCLUSION
  LIST CAREFULLY: live performance goes to NoteSipari or Orizzonti L.I.V.E.
 \, exhibition-format initiatives and film festivals go to Immagini e Prosp
 ettive\, heritage restoration goes to BeST\, and accessible territorial-sh
 owcase events go to Eventi for All\, so Ordinarie is the residual arts rou
 te. Non-profit entities and institutions operating in the reference territ
 ory are eligible\, and because the applicant does not need to be headquart
 ered in Piedmont or Valle d'Aosta this is genuinely open to organisations 
 based elsewhere\, including non-EU and UK\, that run a programme in those 
 regions. The project route has two deadlines: the first was 30 April 2026 
 and the second session is open 1 July to 15 October 2026 at 15:00 Italian 
 time. Organisations receiving an activity-support grant cannot also benefi
 t from other CRT calls in the same calendar year. Applications are made th
 rough rol.fondazionecrt.it.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione CRT (Fondazione Ca
 ssa di Risparmio di Torino)\nLocation: Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy.
  The project must be delivered in those regions\, but the applicant does n
 ot need to be headquartered there.\nAward: No published fixed minimum or m
 aximum for the arts strand\; grant size is set case by case against the pr
 oject budget and the applicant's financial capacity. Co-financing is not u
 niversally mandated but specific categories carry thresholds (conference a
 nd seminar requests above EUR 10\,000 are inadmissible without co-financin
 g of at least two thirds of budgeted spend). Across all three areas Fondaz
 ione CRT distributed roughly EUR 5.5 million to 349 projects in a single r
 ecent Ordinarie session. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; gr
 ant-use period governed by the Regolamento Generale di Erogazione 2026\, w
 ith extensions of up to 12 months available on request.\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/arte-cultura-ordinarie/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/arte-cultura-ordinarie/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. The project must be delivered 
 in those regions\, but the applicant does not need to be headquartered the
 re.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:perform-europe-third-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Perform Europe: Third Open Call for Cross-Border Touring 
 (2026-28 edition)
DESCRIPTION:Perform Europe is the EU's dedicated cross-border touring schem
 e for the performing arts\, run by a six-organisation consortium and co-fu
 nded by Creative Europe. It funds partnerships of at least three organisat
 ions from three different Creative Europe countries to tour a finished per
 forming arts work in at least three countries\, with an explicit emphasis 
 on greener\, more inclusive and more equitable touring practice. Eligible 
 disciplines are circus\, dance\, outdoor arts\, performance art\, puppetry
  and theatre\; LIVE MUSIC AND OPERA ARE EXCLUDED\, and production costs fo
 r new creations are not covered since the work must already be finished be
 fore 1 March 2027. Applicants pick one of three grant tiers with no fixed 
 criteria per tier\, and may request up to EUR 5\,000 in top-ups for access
 ibility and sustainability measures. Five percent of the total fund is rin
 g-fenced for proposals involving Ukrainian partners or supporting the Ukra
 inian performing arts sector. All 41 Creative Europe countries are eligibl
 e\, including Albania\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Icela
 nd\, Kosovo\, Liechtenstein\, Moldova\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Nor
 way\, Serbia\, Tunisia and Ukraine\, but the UK is not. TIMING: applicatio
 ns close 22 October 2026 at 23:59 CEST\, selected partnerships are announc
 ed in January 2027\, and activity may only start from 1 March 2027. A Matc
 hmaking Platform with over 2\,300 registered professionals is available fo
 r finding partners before applying. CORE PRIORITY: each partnership must p
 ick either diversity and inclusion or the fight against climate change as 
 its core priority\, and must also include measures addressing the other on
 e\; that choice has to run visibly through the whole application rather th
 an sit in one section. WHO COUNTS AS A PARTNER: both organisations and ind
 ividual professionals are eligible\, so a partner can be an artist\, colle
 ctive\, company\, producer\, presenter\, venue\, festival\, residency\, ed
 ucational institution or NGO. Eligibility is decided by where you are lega
 lly based. The partnership appoints a lead partner who submits\, signs and
  receives the grant. ELIGIBLE COSTS: artistic fees and salaries\, travel\,
  accommodation\, subsistence\, administration\, reporting\, communication\
 , translation\, surtitling\, equipment transport\, copyright fees\, access
  and environmental measures\, complementary activities and capacity buildi
 ng. Venue and equipment rental or purchase is capped at 5 percent of the r
 equested grant\, and preparation costs for presenting an existing work at 
 10 percent. PAYMENT: 60 percent after signing\, 20 percent after the first
  narrative and financial report is approved\, and the final 20 percent aft
 er completion and EU approval of Perform Europe's own final report. Top-up
 s are reimbursed only after the project ends and documentation is approved
 \, so budget for the cash-flow gap. PRACTICAL: every partner must register
  for a Perform Europe account before submission and approval can take seve
 ral working days\, so do not leave that to the last week.\n\nOrganisation:
  Perform Europe (IETM\, EFA\, Circostrada\, European Dancehouse Network\, 
 Pearle*\, IDEA Consult)\, co-funded by Creative Europe\nLocation: Europe-w
 ide\; touring must happen in at least 3 Creative Europe countries. The UK 
 is NOT eligible.\nAward: Three grant tiers of EUR 15\,000\, EUR 25\,000 or
  EUR 55\,000\, plus top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000\, giving a EUR 60\,000 cei
 ling per partnership. EUR 1.4 million total across at least 25 partnership
 s\, covering up to 100 percent of eligible costs\, so no matching funds ar
 e needed. TOP-UP RATES: green mobility EUR 400 per person per presentation
  date\; accessibility support EUR 400 per person per presentation date\; f
 amily top-up EUR 200 per child per presentation date\; audience access EUR
  800 per presentation date\; visa EUR 120 per person needing one\; oversea
 s and outermost regions EUR 175 per person per presentation date. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Touring and implementation 1 March 2027 to 31 Janua
 ry 2028 (11 months).\n\nMore: https://performeurope.eu/open-call/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://performeurope.eu/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe-wide\; touring must happen in at least 3 Creative Europe co
 untries. The UK is NOT eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-rotterdam-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Rotterdam: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsi
 die Cultuur\, September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Rotterdam's standing project fund for one-off artistic and cult
 ural activity\, and the most accessible municipal route for festivals\, ex
 hibitions and public programmes in the city. The discipline list names e-c
 ulture outright alongside moving image and artistic film\, design and fash
 ion\, visual arts and photography\, architecture\, spoken word and all hyb
 rid forms\, so media-art and creative-technology programming is squarely i
 n scope. Both non-profit legal entities and natural persons may apply\, so
  individual artists are eligible. There is no published maximum per applic
 ation\; the real constraint is the EUR 272\,000 available per round agains
 t roughly 130 competing applications. Six rounds run every year with fixed
  closing dates on the first of January\, March\, May\, July\, September an
 d November. TIMING RULE: the activity may not start until eight weeks afte
 r the closing date of the round applied in\, so a 1 September 2026 applica
 tion supports activity from late October 2026 onward. Decisions normally a
 rrive within eight weeks of the round deadline\, extendable to 20 weeks. A
 ssociations and foundations apply via eHerkenning\, individuals via DigiD.
  Organisations already receiving Rotterdamse Culturele Basis\, Cultuurplan
 \, Impulsregeling\, national BIS\, Lokale Culturele Programmering or a CBK
  Rotterdam practice contribution are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente R
 otterdam (Municipality of Rotterdam)\nLocation: Activity must serve a Rott
 erdam interest and take place in or for Rotterdam. City-restricted by rele
 vance of the activity rather than by applicant address.\nAward: No stated 
 per-application cap. Annual pot EUR 1\,632\,000 split into six rounds of E
 UR 272\,000\, with roughly 130 applications per round. Discipline sub-caps
 : book writing max EUR 4\,500\; moving image R&D max EUR 4\,000\; moving-i
 mage production max EUR 12\,500\; post-production max EUR 4\,000. Applican
 ts must demonstrably seek other funds or sponsors. Awards over EUR 50\,000
  require an auditor's statement at reporting\, at the applicant's cost. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Single one-off project.\n\nMore: https://www.
 rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must serve a Rotterdam interest and take place in or for 
 Rotterdam. City-restricted by relevance of the activity rather than by app
 licant address.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstraad-groningen-tweejarige-programmaregeling-2027@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kunstraad Groningen: Two-Year Programme Scheme (Tweejarig
 e Programmaregeling\, 2027-2028)
DESCRIPTION:This is the Groningen scheme that actually funds festivals\, an
 d the correct counterpart to the Kunstraad's Projectenregeling\, which exp
 licitly excludes festivals and recurring programmes and redirects them her
 e. It supports coherent\, continuous public activity across 2027 and 2028 
 in all arts and heritage disciplines\, naming recurring production series\
 , festivals and programme lines as eligible\, with no exclusion of media a
 rt\, digital culture or experimental sound work. Annually recurring festiv
 als with a year-round paid organisation are explicitly named as eligible a
 pplicants. Awards run from EUR 5\,000 to 40\,000 per year against an annua
 l pot of EUR 325\,000\, capped at one third of total project costs\, so tw
 o thirds must come from municipal funds\, national funds\, box office or o
 wn contribution. Unusually\, the money may also be used to strengthen the 
 organisation itself on the business side\, not only to pay for programme c
 ontent. The application window is 1 July to 1 September 2026\, closing at 
 23:59\, and only applications received on time are processed. Applications
  must be submitted in Dutch via the Mijn Kunstraad portal with fair-pay st
 andards applied in the budget. Funding covers nothing before 1 January 202
 7. Professional non-profit organisations only\; amateur associations and i
 ndividual artists are directed elsewhere. Material investments\, equipment
  purchases and housing costs are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Kunstraad Gron
 ingen\, on behalf of the municipality and province of Groningen\nLocation:
  Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation must b
 e based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 min
 imum to EUR 40\,000 maximum per year across two years\, so up to EUR 80\,0
 00 total. Covers a maximum of one third of total project costs\, requiring
  roughly 67 percent co-financing. Annual scheme budget EUR 325\,000. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, covering 2027 and 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmare
 geling/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmaregeling/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation
  must be based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondspodiumkunsten-buitenlandse-voorstellingen-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Podiumkunsten: Foreign Performances or Concerts in 
 the Netherlands (round 4\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Fonds Podiumkunsten's route for Dutch festivals and venues brin
 ging in exceptional foreign performing arts and concerts that Dutch audien
 ces would otherwise not see. The applicant must be a Netherlands-registere
 d legal entity running a venue or festival and carrying artistic and finan
 cial responsibility for its own programme\, so individuals and sole trader
 s cannot apply. Grants are calculated from travel and transport costs of t
 he incoming artists\, at a maximum of EUR 25\,000 per production and EUR 7
 5\,000 per applicant across several productions. The core test is that the
  foreign work is rarely or never seen in the Netherlands and substantially
  enriches the existing Dutch offer\, which favours experimental\, non-cano
 nical and cross-disciplinary programming over mainstream touring. Experime
 ntal music and sound-art programming is not excluded\; the selection crite
 rion is rarity and added value\, not genre. Applications go through the Mi
 jn Fonds portal and there is no fee. Four rounds run each year. TIMING: be
 cause the scheme competes against a shared EUR 267\,500 per-round pot and 
 assessment takes several weeks after the deadline\, organisers should appl
 y at least one full round ahead of the performance date and must not have 
 the activity already underway. Success rate in 2025 was 60 percent of 33 a
 pplications.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Podiumkunsten (Performing Arts Fund NL
 )\nLocation: Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from 
 Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are als
 o in scope. No city or region restriction.\nAward: Maximum EUR 25\,000 per
  production\, capped at EUR 75\,000 for an applicant presenting multiple p
 roductions. Calculated on travel and transport costs of the foreign artist
 s and their production only. EUR 267\,500 available per round shared acros
 s this scheme and two sibling internationalisation schemes. Fees\, venue a
 nd production costs stay with the applicant. No application fee.\nDuration
 : Single performances or a short run of concerts within one programme or f
 estival edition.\n\nMore: https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenla
 ndse-voorstellingen-of-concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenlandse-voorstellingen-of-
 concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from Aruba
 \, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are also in 
 scope. No city or region restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-utrecht-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Utrecht: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsidi
 e Cultuur\, round 3 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht's main project fund for cultural activity with a public
  presentation in the city\, covering all art forms including experimental 
 and cross-disciplinary work. Individuals\, foundations\, associations and 
 companies are all eligible. Two bands apply: Category A of EUR 1\,000 to 5
 \,000 assessed on artistic importance and entrepreneurship\, and Category 
 B of EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 which adds meaning for the city as a third crit
 erion. The activity must be exceptional or innovative\, or otherwise of va
 lue to the city\, its residents or the Utrecht cultural sector\; professio
 nal projects and amateur\, education or participation projects both qualif
 y. Three rounds run each year and the next closes 25 September 2026 at 17:
 00 CET. TIMING RULE\, which catches applicants out: for professional arts 
 applications the presentation may not take place earlier than 13 weeks aft
 er the round's closing date\, and for participatory applications the proje
 ct may not start earlier than 13 weeks after that date\, so a 25 September
  2026 application supports activity from late December 2026 onward. Decisi
 ons are issued no later than 13 weeks after the closing date\, following r
 eview by an independent Adviescommissie Projectsubsidies. Documentation is
  capped at 15 pages\, or 5 pages if a video is included. Applications go t
 hrough mijnsubsidie.utrecht.nl with DigiD or eHerkenning. Utrecht also run
 s a rolling Impulssubsidie Cultuur of up to EUR 2\,500 for first-time appl
 icants only\, open through 31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente Utr
 echt (Municipality of Utrecht)\nLocation: Activity must have a presentatio
 n moment in Utrecht and benefit residents of the municipality of Utrecht. 
 City-restricted by presentation location\, not by applicant residence.\nAw
 ard: Category A: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000. Category B: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000. 
 No fixed co-financing percentage\, but a budget and coverage plan is manda
 tory. eHerkenning purchase costs may be included in the budget and are rei
 mbursed if awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project.\n\nMore
 : https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-a
 anvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-
 aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must have a presentation moment in Utrecht and benefit re
 sidents of the municipality of Utrecht. City-restricted by presentation lo
 cation\, not by applicant residence.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bng-cultuurfonds-projectsubsidies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: BNG Cultuurfonds: Project Grants (round closing September
  2026)
DESCRIPTION:BNG Cultuurfonds funds arts and culture projects that add value
  for Dutch municipalities and their inhabitants\, explicitly including tem
 porary exhibitions\, public programmes and festivals developed by professi
 onal makers. Media art\, digital culture and cross-disciplinary work quali
 fy as long as a professional maker's artistic vision leads the project. On
 ly stichtingen (foundations) may apply: no sole traders\, associations\, i
 ndividuals\, or foundations in formation. Applications go by email to aanv
 raag.cultuurfonds@bngbank.nl with a signed form\, a project plan of at mos
 t 3\,500 words\, a specified budget and coverage plan\, current statutes a
 nd a recent KvK extract. The grant is EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000 and can cover 
 no more than 35 percent of the budget. TIMING IS THE MAIN TRAP: for the 27
  September 2026 deadline\, feedback comes at the end of December 2026 and 
 the project may not start before 1 January 2027\, with applications for ea
 rlier-starting projects rejected outright with no exceptions. Missing docu
 ments are flagged up to one week before the deadline\, so anything submitt
 ed in the final week cannot be corrected. Plan for roughly four months of 
 lead time. Excluded: amateur art\, talent development\, education-focused 
 projects\, semi-permanent public art\, publications\, building or renovati
 on\, and regular operating costs. Further rounds: 3 January 2027\, 28 Marc
 h 2027\, 27 June 2027\, 3 October 2027 and 2 January 2028.\n\nOrganisation
 : Stichting BNG Cultuurfonds (BNG Bank)\nLocation: Project must take place
  in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely abroad are excluded. Not regio
 n-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Limburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe an
 d Zeeland.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 minimum to EUR 15\,000 maximum. The request 
 must represent 5 to 35 percent of total project funding\, so at least 65 p
 ercent co-financing is required. The fund is never the sole financier\, an
 d place-specific projects require at least one local or regional co-financ
 ier. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project with a clear start and 
 end\; must be executed within two years of award. A grantee cannot reapply
  for 36 months.\n\nMore: https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsu
 bsidies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsubsidies?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Project must take place in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely
  abroad are excluded. Not region-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Li
 mburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe and Zeeland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuur-eindhoven-projecten-2027-r1@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven: Project Subsidy (Projecten\,
  2027 round 1)
DESCRIPTION:The mid-size project strand of Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\, th
 e arm's-length body that distributes the city's culture budget\, and the m
 ain municipal route for an Eindhoven organisation to fund a festival\, exh
 ibition or public programme. Awards go up to EUR 35\,000 and cover a maxim
 um of 80 percent of eligible costs\, so at least a fifth of the budget mus
 t come from elsewhere. Unlike the Snelgeld strand this route is closed to 
 individuals: only private-law legal entities established in Eindhoven may 
 apply. Rounds run three times a year in fixed windows\; the next opens 1 S
 eptember and closes at 17:00 on 30 September 2026\, which is round 1 of th
 e 2027 cycle. TIMING: the decision lag is long by municipal standards at u
 p to 13 weeks after the submission window closes\, so a September 2026 app
 lication is decided around the end of December 2026 and activity should be
  planned for 2027. Given Eindhoven's design and technology profile\, media
 -art\, design and creative-technology programming fits the remit particula
 rly well. The parallel Snelgeld strand offers up to EUR 5\,000 on rolling 
 intake\, reopening 1 September 2026 and running until 31 December 2026 or 
 until the tranche budget is exhausted\, whichever comes first.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\nLocation: Eindhoven. The applicant must
  be a legal entity based in Eindhoven and the activity must serve the Eind
 hoven cultural offering. City-restricted at the applicant level.\nAward: M
 aximum EUR 35\,000 per application and maximum 80 percent of eligible cost
 s\, so at least 20 percent co-financing is required. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Single project within the 2025-2028 policy period.\n\nMore: http
 s://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Eindhoven. The applicant must be a legal entity based in Eindhoven
  and the activity must serve the Eindhoven cultural offering. City-restric
 ted at the applicant level.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-den-haag-kunst-cultuurprojecten-b-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Den Haag: Arts and Culture Projects Category B (
 autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The larger of The Hague's two municipal project bands and the a
 ppropriate route for an organisation running a festival or substantial pub
 lic programme in the city. Awards range from EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 agains
 t an annual ceiling of EUR 600\,000 for the whole strand. THE CO-FINANCING
  REQUIREMENT IS SEVERE and is the single most important planning constrain
 t: the municipal culture budget may fund at most 30 percent of the total p
 roject budget\, so an applicant seeking EUR 30\,000 must already have roug
 hly EUR 70\,000 secured or plausibly projected elsewhere. Only legal entit
 ies may apply\; individuals and informal collectives must use Category A i
 nstead (EUR 2\,000 to 10\,000\, 70 percent coverage ceiling\, next window 
 1 to 15 September 2026). Professional arts and culture organisations runni
 ng public projects in music\, theatre\, dance\, film\, literature\, visual
  arts or combinations are eligible. The next window opens 1 October and cl
 oses at 17:00 on 15 October 2026. TIMING: the decision term is 12 weeks af
 ter the window closes\, so an October 2026 application is decided around e
 arly January 2027 and activity should be scheduled from 2027 onward. Appli
 cations are handled through the municipality's subsidy system\, which migr
 ated to Easyfunders in April 2026. This scheme is independent of Stroom De
 n Haag. The underlying regulation runs to 31 December 2028.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Gemeente Den Haag (Municipality of The Hague)\nLocation: The Hague. App
 licant must be active in Den Haag and the project must be publicly accessi
 ble there. City-restricted.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 per application
 . The municipal culture-budget contribution may not exceed 30 percent of t
 he total project budget\, so at least 70 percent co-financing is required.
  Annual ceiling for the strand is EUR 600\,000. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Maximum one year per project.\n\nMore: https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subs
 idies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/subsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-
 aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subsidies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/su
 bsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague. Applicant must be active in Den Haag and the project mu
 st be publicly accessible there. City-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle. Both arts-sector organisations an
 d individual arts professionals may apply\, though the applicant needs a b
 ank account and legal footing and cannot be a BIS-funded institution. The 
 project must centre on performing artists in the copyright sense\, meaning
  people who perform a copyright-protected work: musicians\, dancers\, acto
 rs\, voice actors. This fits live experimental music\, sound performance a
 nd performative media-art work\, but not object-based exhibitions or non-p
 erformative installation programmes. The maximum grant is EUR 10\,000\, th
 e total project budget must stay under EUR 150\,000\, the applicant's annu
 al budget under EUR 500\,000\, and at least a quarter of the project budge
 t must be earned from audience income\, so this is a top-up rather than a 
 primary funding source. Budgets must honour NORMA's 2026 performer wage no
 rms. Applications are submitted online during a one-month window each quar
 ter\; the next round runs 1 to 30 October 2026\, closing at 23:59. TIMING 
 RULE: decisions arrive no later than eight weeks after the deadline\, and 
 the premiere date must fall at least eight weeks after the application dea
 dline. Organisations that already received a NORMA Fonds grant in 2024 or 
 2025 are excluded\, and supporting staff may not exceed 2 FTE.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting NORMA (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restriction s
 tated.\nAward: Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may n
 ot exceed EUR 150\,000 and the applicant organisation's annual budget may 
 not exceed EUR 500\,000. At least 25 percent of the project budget must co
 me from audience or box-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 
 wage norms of EUR 139 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Single project\, typically a production or concert s
 eries. Final report due within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://
 www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturstiftung-des-bundes-general-project-funding-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturstiftung des Bundes: General Project Funding (Allge
 meine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Germany's flagship open\, non-thematic federal project line\, a
 nd one of the largest European funders that will back a festival\, exhibit
 ion programme or multi-partner convening run by an organisation rather tha
 n an individual artist. It funds large innovative projects across all arti
 stic fields\, explicitly including New Media alongside visual and performi
 ng arts\, music\, film\, photography and architecture. There is no publish
 ed maximum\, but the EUR 50\,000 minimum total project cost sets the scale
 \, and at least 20 percent co-financing is mandatory. Deadlines are twice 
 yearly at 12:00 CET: 31 July 2026 and 31 January 2027. TIMING RULE: decisi
 ons are made by an external jury meeting in May and November\, and no proj
 ect may start before its jury date\, so plan four to six months of lead ti
 me. Non-German organisations are genuinely eligible\, which is unusual at 
 this scale\, provided the project is visible in Germany and has an interna
 tional dimension. Two practical barriers: the application form must be com
 pleted in German\, and project communications must include a German-langua
 ge version.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturstiftung des Bundes (German Federal Cul
 tural Foundation)\nLocation: Activity must be visible to audiences in Germ
 any. Institutions headquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.\nAward: No
  fixed ceiling\, but total project costs must exceed EUR 50\,000 to be eli
 gible. The Foundation allocates up to EUR 10 million per year across this 
 line. At least 20 percent of total project costs must be secured from own 
 capital and/or third-party funding. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -length. Projects may not begin before the jury meeting.\n\nMore: https://
 www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_project_funding
 .html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_proj
 ect_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions hea
 dquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-point-network-funding-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Point: Short-term Network Funding\, Nordic
 -Baltic Mobility Programme (autumn 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Supports organisations building new cross-border professional n
 etworks\, funding joint meetings\, workshops\, staff exchanges and collabo
 rative platforms among artists and cultural practitioners. It is designed 
 for the convening and infrastructure-building side of festival work rather
  than artistic production\, and it explicitly excludes artistic production
 s and public events\, so it is used to assemble festival partners rather t
 han to stage the festival itself. Grants run up to EUR 20\,000 for network
 s of a year or less\, with Nordic Culture Point covering at most 70 percen
 t of the budget and a hard 85 percent ceiling on combined pan-Nordic publi
 c funding. The autumn 2026 window is 10 August to 4 September 2026\, closi
 ng 15:59 UTC+3. TIMING RULE: activity may not begin until at least eight w
 eeks after the deadline. IMPORTANT ELIGIBILITY DIFFERENCE from the Culture
  and Art Programme: the applicant must be resident in a Nordic or Baltic c
 ountry and must be a professional with documented training or experience i
 n art and culture\, so non-Nordic and non-Baltic lead applicants are not e
 ligible. A strong fit for a media-arts or sound-art organisation assemblin
 g a regional partner consortium ahead of a larger application.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Nordic Culture Point (Kulturkontakt Nord)\nLocation: Nordic and Balt
 ic region. The network must include partners from at least three of: Denma
 rk\, Estonia\, Finland\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Iceland\, Latvia\, Li
 thuania\, Norway\, Sweden\, Aland.\nAward: Up to EUR 20\,000 for networks 
 lasting one year or less. Nordic Culture Point covers a maximum of 70 perc
 ent of the project budget\, and combined funding from this programme plus 
 other pan-Nordic bodies may not exceed 85 percent\, so at least 15 percent
  must come from other sources. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to one ye
 ar. Activity may start no earlier than eight weeks after the deadline.\n\n
 More: https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/short-term-network-funding/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/short-term-network-funding/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nordic and Baltic region. The network must include partners from a
 t least three of: Denmark\, Estonia\, Finland\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\
 , Iceland\, Latvia\, Lithuania\, Norway\, Sweden\, Aland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-point-culture-art-programme-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Point: Culture and Art Programme (autumn 2
 026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Nordic Culture Point's main project line\, funding Nordic colla
 borative arts and culture projects across all phases: preliminary work\, p
 roduction\, presentation and dissemination. Eligible activity explicitly i
 ncludes creative productions\, workshops\, knowledge development and space
 s for artists to meet publics\, which covers festivals\, public programmes
  and convenings when framed as new collaborations. The tiered co-financing
  model is the standout feature: EUR 7\,000 with no match at all\, rising t
 o EUR 100\,000 at a 50 percent match\, and in-kind contributions count. NO
 TABLE: applicants do not need Nordic residency or citizenship provided the
  three-country and two-Nordic partner structure is met\, so a non-Nordic o
 rganisation can lead the project. The autumn window runs 10 August to 10 S
 eptember 2026\, closing 15:59 UTC+3. TIMING RULE: decisions arrive ten wee
 ks after the deadline and no project may start before notification\, so bu
 dget for a roughly three-month lag. The programme will not finance existin
 g tours\, institutional running costs\, ongoing festival core financing\, 
 solo performances\, film\, TV or gaming production\, or book publishing\, 
 so a recurring festival must present a distinct new collaborative strand r
 ather than seek operating support.\n\nOrganisation: Nordic Culture Point (
 Kulturkontakt Nord)\nLocation: Activity may take place anywhere\, but the 
 project must involve partners with addresses in at least three different c
 ountries\, at least two of which are Nordic (Denmark\, Finland\, Iceland\,
  Norway\, Sweden\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Aland).\nAward: Tiered by c
 o-financing: up to EUR 7\,000 with NO co-funding required\; up to EUR 40\,
 000 with at least 30 percent co-funding\; up to EUR 100\,000 with at least
  50 percent co-funding. In-kind goods and services count toward co-financi
 ng. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based. Funded activity may only
  begin after decision notification\, roughly ten weeks after the deadline.
 \n\nMore: https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/culture-and-art-programme/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/culture-and-art-programme/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place anywhere\, but the project must involve pa
 rtners with addresses in at least three different countries\, at least two
  of which are Nordic (Denmark\, Finland\, Iceland\, Norway\, Sweden\, Faro
 e Islands\, Greenland\, Aland).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T184925Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
 Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subs
 idy of EUR 9\,188 for an artist or EUR 7\,232 for a curator/art observer t
 oward travel\, material and living costs (a 10 percent personal contributi
 on is automatically deducted by the Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living spac
 e and Delfina Foundation support are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. 
 Contribution for Caribbean-based artists can be increased for higher trave
 l costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 27 September to 17 D
 ecember 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/g
 rants/residency/delfina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/del
 fina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherla
 nds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
